[Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  i saw this story i wanted to bring in  jeff passing  the new york mets general manager jared  porter acknowledges sending explicit  images to a female reporter when he  worked for the chicago cubs  i believe this is back in 2016. he was  hired  by the mets to be their general manager  he is no longer the mets general manager  because he has been fired  and jeff passin from the mother ship who  covers baseball joining us on the  program when did you get  first word about this uh something that  was done in  back in 2016 with the cubs  me personally dan was very recently okay  but  uh my colleague mina kimes uh  first was given the text back in 2017  december of 2017 and  uh went and met with the woman and  talked with her about possibly  doing a story on this at the time she  was not ready for that she was still  working in the journalism industry and  she was afraid that the blowback from a  story being published was going to  significantly harm her career  she is no longer in journalism and as  she saw  jared porter's ascent to general manager  of the mets  you know it hit her there's a person who  did something to me  and his career is on an upward  trajectory  i'm the victim in this situation and i  now don't have my dream job anymore  why is this fair why is this okay why is  uh from all i can gather dan  the mets found out when we told them  that we were going to be publishing this  story yesterday  that they did not know about this  beforehand that it caught them  off guard you know inside of baseball  let's go back to 2016 with the cubs  there was one other person in the cubs  organization at the time  who found out about it afterward because  the woman had  gone to her employer and someone at her  employer had called up  somebody with the cubs uh who that  person knew  and that person with whom we spoke  yesterday  said that he was trying to essentially  be a go-between to bring the woman  and porter together to have some kind of  a resolution for this that never  happened she was considering  legal action at the time she says that  he was pushing her not to pursue legal  action  um how many texts messages did he send  this woman  in total it was a hundred fifty or so  the the majority of those were at the  beginning they had met at yankee stadium  and she thought hey you know we're going  to talk baseball he's going to be a  source that's what reporters do  trying to cultivate sources but very  quickly  uh the the messages from porter went  beyond the normal  source relationship to a point where he  was asking her out  trying to get her to come and visit him  in different places across the country  and after he sent one particular picture  uh which he says wasn't him but was uh  of a man  laying on a bed with a bulge in his  pants uh she stopped responding  after she stopped responding there were  more than 60 texts  from jared porter that culminated  uh with a picture of a naked penis  and that is where we are and that is  ultimately i think  uh what got him fired not just the the  lewd image itself  but the fact that it came after she had  not responded to  60 plus texts what's uh the reaction  from uh  the new owner steve cohen i mean you saw  it this  morning he got fired before 8 a.m  eastern and this was a story that was  published about 11 o'clock last night so  it didn't even  take half a day and steve cohen if you  remember in his initial press conference  said we want this to be an organization  of integrity and he referenced that  again  this morning in the tweet uh in which he  announced the firing publicly he said i  want to run this organization with  integrity and  uh we could not do that with him in  charge  and this had been a pretty good  off-season with the trade getting lindor  from cleveland uh they helped their  pitching staff here  um and i go back to last year with  carlos beltran does beltron get another  chance here jeff well aj hinch has  gotten another chance no  i know that's why alex scores alex cora  has gotten another chance  it stands to reason that carlos beltran  would get another chance considering the  other two who have  yeah just trying to figure that out  because that was with the mets as well  um are they a cursed organization  do we look at them sort of the the way  we do the knicks  dan i'm from cleveland so if anyone's  going to believe in curry if anyone's  going to believe in curses  it's me and i still do not believe in  the idea of a cursed organization what i  do believe in is the idea of culture  and that culture can perpetuate itself  through a place and metastasize  and that getting rid of that cancer  inside of an organization can take a  really  long time but but it's possible like  let's not look past the idea that the  new york mets  can one day become a functional  organization  if things are done correctly and in  something like this you know  when you make a mistake you can either  double down on it  or you can acknowledge quickly that it  was a mistake  and i i think the mets did so in this  case and that's a good  first step in writing the error of your  ways  good to visit with you you and mina did  a great job a deep dive on this at  espn.com thank you jeff  my pleasure to have you jeff panson espn  baseball insider

